    "title": "These 6 Devastating Closures Are Missed Most by Idaho Foodies - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Shannon ,\n11 hours ago Credit: Google Maps Local spots in Boise are what make this city one of the best to live in for foodies. On almost every corner or on every street you’re sure to find some of your local food favorites. Just as exciting as it is to try new places some of the local restaurants have been around for years and years. While everyone has their local faves one of the hardest parts is when it shuts down.\nSadly it is been hard to watch as many local restaurants, cafes, and diners have all closed down here in Boise. Regular customers are crushed when their favorite restaurants are no longer open and their favorite food places are no longer available to eat at.\nWe were curious to see which local restaurants and food places were the ones that people missed the most. It gives us hope that maybe one day these places that still have fans may return just in a new location.\nWhat Boise Spots Are Locals Missing Locals share there input. Gallery Credit: Shannon Buccola What's A Boise Spot You Miss That's No Longer Around What spot's do you miss? Wild Waters Did you go here? Donnie Mac's Did you like this? Ben's Crow Inn They miss it. Credit: Canva and 103.5 KISS FM via Facebook Primo's Pizza Did you like their pizza? Credit: Canva and 103.5 KISS FM via Facebook Joe's Crab Shack Do you wish for their return? Credit: Canva and 103.5 KISS FM via Facebook Farms and No Californians They are sarcastic. People had all sorts of favorites that they were missing including chains like The Cheesecake Factory. Its hard when places you’ve grown to love end up leaving town but considering so many new ones get added we’re lucky that there’s always great food options in the area. That’s part of the reason why Boise is always a great spot for foodies.\nLuckily there’s likely new local places that you haven’t even tried yet. If you’re looking for some new local spots to try we also recently asked what everyone’s favorites were and this is what the Boise community had to say:\nHidden Gem Restaurants in Boise Have you tried these local spots? Gallery Credit: Shannon Buccola Credit: Facebook/103.5 KISS FM What's The Best Hidden Gem Restaurant in Boie? What will the locals say? Lucky Palace It's in Boise. Credit: Facebook/103.5 KISS FM Chefs Hut This sounds yummy. Credit: Facebook/103.5 KISS FM Express Cafe Have you tried it? Mancino's Pizza and Grinders Pizza and sandwiches! Credit: Facebook/103.5 KISS FM Sunflower Bakery and Cafe It's in Meridian. Credit: Facebook/103.5 KISS FM Zee's Rooftop Food and a view! El Gallo Giro Are you hungry? Where Boise Residents Go For Lunch Where would you go? Gallery Credit: Shannon Buccola Credit: Canva The Question This was asked on Facebook. Credit: Facebook/103.5 KISS FM The Answers Baguette Deli Credit: Facebook/103.5 KISS FM The Answers In N Out Credit: Facebook/103.5 KISS FM The Answers Fiesta Chicken or Tangos. Credit: Facebook/103.5 KISS FM The Answers Don and Charley's Credit: Facebook/103.5 KISS FM The Answers Panda Express. Credit: Facebook/103.5 KISS FM The Answers Tangos or Boise Fry Co. Credit: Facebook/103.5 KISS FM The Answers Credit: Facebook/103.5 KISS FM The Answers Home",
